{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-148",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "One combined diagram of four convenient rays from A to a concave spherical mirror and the downward image A_1B_1. O means curvature center. First-order paraxial convergence, not exact spherical focusing. Vertical scale is explicitly enlarged. The lower contact C is resolved by the retained independent SOURCE186 detail observation; historical author uncertainty is preserved separately.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/10p/figures/fig-148.png",
      "sha256": "e69ddc9f8bbeffa3e2b8ed3738f8ac513a7ea90af618ee29f9147c38a0a0b23c"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "If the position of an object relative to a spherical mirror is known, a ray construction can locate its **image**.\nFirst construct the image of an individual point, using a ruler and compass to determine the reflected ray paths.\nThe focusing constructions below use the paraxial approximation."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "To construct the reflected path of the incident ray $AC$, draw a secondary optical axis parallel to $AC$ (Figure 147).\nThis secondary axis meets the focal plane at $D$.\nThe line through the point of incidence $C$ and $D$ gives the reflected ray path."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "The construction follows from the fact that paraxial rays parallel to the same secondary axis meet at one point in the focal plane after reflection.\nFollowing just one of these rays is enough to locate that point.\nChoose the ray through the center of curvature $O$, along the secondary axis itself.\n\nThis ray retraces its straight path after reflection, so its reflected path also passes through the unknown point $D$.\nThus $D$ lies in both the focal plane and the secondary axis: it is their intersection."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "To construct the image of an object point $A$, use the following convenient rays (Figure 148)."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "1. The ray $AOC$ through the center of curvature $O$ retraces the same straight path $COA$ after reflection."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "2. The ray $AFK$ through the focus is reflected parallel to the principal axis."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "3. The ray $AP$ strikes the pole of the mirror; its reflected ray is symmetric to the incident ray about the principal axis."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "4. The incident ray $AE$ is parallel to the principal axis; its reflected path $EFA_1$ passes through the focus."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "In the paraxial imaging model shown, rays from $A$ that reflect from the mirror pass through the image point $A_1$.\nChoose **any two** of the convenient rays to locate $A_1$.\nThe other reflected rays pass through the same image point.\n\nA real mirror may not reflect every convenient ray.\nFor example, some medical concave mirrors have a hole at the center, so a ray reaching the hole is not reflected.\nThe image can still be constructed using rays reflected by the remaining reflecting surface."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "To construct the image of an entire object, it is enough to construct the images of points on its **outline**."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "知道物体相对球面镜的位置后，就可以通过作图确定**像的位置**。\n先作出物体上任意一点的像，再用直尺和圆规确定光线反射后的方向。\n下面的聚焦作图采用近轴光线的近似。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "作出入射光线 $AC$ 的反射线时，先画一条与 $AC$ 平行的副光轴（图 147）。\n这条副光轴与镜子的焦平面相交于点 $D$。\n从镜面上的入射点 $C$ 经过 $D$ 的直线，就是所求的反射光路。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "这个作图法的根据是：平行于同一副光轴的近轴光线，反射后会聚在焦平面上的同一点。\n只需研究其中一条光线，就能找到这个点。\n可以选择通过镜子曲率中心 $O$、与副光轴重合的光线。\n\n这条光线反射后沿原来的直线返回，所以它的反射光路也经过未知点 $D$。\n因此，$D$ 同时在焦平面和这条副光轴上，是它们的交点。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "要作出物体上任意一点 $A$ 的像，可以选用以下光线（图 148）。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "1. 经过曲率中心 $O$ 的光线 $AOC$，反射后的光路 $COA$ 沿原来的直线返回。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "2. 经过镜子焦点的光线 $AFK$，反射后平行于主光轴。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "3. 射到镜子顶点的光线 $AP$，其反射线与入射线关于主光轴对称。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "4. 平行于主光轴的入射光线 $AE$，反射后的光路 $EFA_1$ 经过焦点。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "在图示的近轴成像模型中，从 $A$ 射到镜子的光线反射后都通过像点 $A_1$。\n要定位 $A_1$，选上面光线中的**任意两条**即可。\n其余入射光线反射后也经过同一像点。\n\n实际镜子未必能反射每一种所选光线。\n例如，有的医用凹面镜中央有小孔，不能反射射到孔里的光线。\n仍可利用有反射面的部分所反射的光线作图成像。"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "phy10-c2-s2-n71",
        "text": "作出整个物体的像时，作出物体**边缘**各点的像就足够了。"
      }
    ],
